<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Simplified Chinese. The folder is the BCP-47 form (b+zh+Hans) rather
     than zh-rCN, so it matches zh-Hans in any region (CN, SG, MY) instead
     of one country; Traditional users fall back to the default English
     until a zh-Hant file exists.

     House lexicon, kept consistent because the app made these words up:
     "goo" (verb) = 捏, "goo" (noun, the work) = 黏糊, UnGoo = 去黏.
     Meltorama 2000 and GOOvie stay in Latin script — they are names, and
     the console's chrome wordmark is the name. -->
